Why? White space.

An isolated crop is tightly bound around a single character (打 or a distractor). It is dense with ink. An 8×8 block of an isolated crop is likely to contain a stroke, so it requires more bits to encode.

A contextual crop is a 100×100 window containing two characters. It has huge margins, the gap between the characters, and empty space above and below. An 8×8 block of a contextual crop is very likely to be pure white paper, which compresses to almost nothing.

The Huffman measurement just proved, deterministically, that the contextual crops contain more structured empty space than the isolated crops. This is the exact kind of named, hand-specified measurement the protocol needed.

